domain DeliveryQualityDefinitionV2:
  description "Revise quality definition revision 1 only for the three completed-review findings."
evidence E1:
  "The owner selected REVISE at Step 4 after review of revision 1 SHA256 3a7380e50ec4aedf8cf6bc730031adbb0a7bbc34820e9b6f0f49590ff0b1931f."
evidence E2:
  "Finding F1 identifies conflict between impact-only recheck wording and the lifecycle rule that changed requirement bytes create a new revision with no inherited review status."
evidence E3:
  "Finding F2 identifies undefined authority and evidence for the waived claim result."
evidence E4:
  "Finding F3 identifies that profile rows do not state how each review instance completes the common eight claim fields."
premise P1:
  "A new snapshot must receive current disposition for every in-scope claim, while unchanged evidence may be reused only after a current-fit check and fresh test execution may remain impact-scoped."
premise P2:
  "Removing waived is smaller and less authority-expanding than designing a waiver system. A desired exception can be expressed by changing the governing requirement through its own owner decision rather than allowing a reviewer to waive it."
premise P3:
  "The delivery profile should be declared as claim templates. The review input must instantiate all eight fields before review, using accepted sources or owner decisions and leaving missing values indeterminate."
premise P4:
  "Revision must preserve the accepted quality dimensions, explicit numerical unknowns, nonblocking optional improvements, and no-new-review-process boundary."
decision D1 based_on E1, E2, E3, E4, P1, P2, P3, P4:
  "Create requirement candidate revision 2 from revision 1 without editing revision 1 or its review. Replace four claim results with conforming, nonconforming, and indeterminate; classify non-applicable material through fixed scope rather than waiver. Define profile rows as templates requiring eight-field instantiation. Require complete current disposition for every new snapshot, allow evidence reuse only after current-fit check, and limit fresh check execution to affected claims."
decision D2 based_on E1, E2, E3, E4, P4:
  "Keep all other definitions, profile criteria, unresolved numerical values, accepted-source dispositions, external names, and later-effect authority unchanged. Produce a new digest and new Step 2 review input. Do not mutate PERT, implementation, commit, push, deploy, or activate."
